From: XR1710G Community
Subject: wifi: mt7996: run common cleanup when a truncated tx-free message ends early

The truncated-message path returned before waking TX, scheduling the
tx worker and consuming the staged free_list, leaking staged skbs and
missing queue recovery. Jump to the common out label instead.
---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1279,7 +1279,7 @@
 		u8 i;
 
 		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end))
-			return;
+			goto out;
 		/* 1'b1: new wcid pair.
 		 * 1'b0: msdu_id with the same 'wcid pair' as above.
 		 */
@@ -1335,6 +1335,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+out:
 	if (wake)
 		mt76_set_tx_blocked(&dev->mt76, false);
 
